*> Values replaced before they are used. Reads in between, partial
*> writes, statements that may read the item unseen, conditional
*> code, the end of the paragraph, and clearing an item before filling
*> it all keep the value.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. STORES.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  TOTAL              PIC 9(5).
01  AMOUNT             PIC 9(5) VALUE 7.
01  REC.
    05  REC-KEY        PIC X(4).
    05  REC-DATA       PIC X(10).
01  REC-ALT REDEFINES REC PIC X(14).
01  NAMES.
    05  NAME-ENTRY     PIC X(8) OCCURS 3.
01  NAME-COUNT         PIC 9 VALUE 1.
01  LIST.
    05  LIST-ENTRY     PIC X OCCURS 1 TO 9 DEPENDING ON NAME-COUNT.
01  OTHER-REC.
    05  REC-KEY        PIC X(4).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
REPLACED.
    MOVE AMOUNT TO TOTAL
    MOVE 1 TO TOTAL
    MOVE REC-ALT TO REC
    DISPLAY AMOUNT.
    MOVE "NEW" TO REC.
CLEARED.
    MOVE 0 TO TOTAL
    MOVE AMOUNT TO TOTAL
    COMPUTE TOTAL = 0
    MOVE AMOUNT TO TOTAL
    MOVE SPACES TO REC
    INITIALIZE REC
    MOVE "  " TO REC-KEY IN REC
    MOVE "ABCD" TO REC-KEY IN REC
    COMPUTE TOTAL = AMOUNT * 0
    MOVE 3 TO TOTAL
    DISPLAY TOTAL REC.
READ-BETWEEN.
    MOVE 9 TO TOTAL
    ADD AMOUNT TO TOTAL
    MOVE 1 TO TOTAL
    DISPLAY TOTAL
    MOVE "AAAA" TO REC-KEY IN REC
    DISPLAY REC
    MOVE "BBBB" TO REC-KEY IN REC
    DISPLAY REC-ALT
    MOVE "CCCC" TO REC-KEY IN REC
    MOVE REC-DATA TO REC-KEY IN REC
    DISPLAY REC.
NOT-FOLLOWED.
    MOVE 6 TO TOTAL
    PERFORM SHOW-TOTAL
    MOVE 1 TO TOTAL
    MOVE 2 TO TOTAL
    IF AMOUNT > 1
        MOVE 3 TO TOTAL
    END-IF
    COMPUTE TOTAL = AMOUNT * 2
        ON SIZE ERROR DISPLAY "TOO BIG"
    END-COMPUTE
    MOVE 4 TO TOTAL
    MOVE "X" TO NAME-ENTRY (1)
    MOVE "Y" TO NAME-ENTRY (1)
    MOVE 5 TO TOTAL.
HIDDEN-READS.
    MOVE 3 TO NAME-COUNT
    MOVE "ABC" TO LIST
    MOVE 9 TO NAME-COUNT
    MOVE "WXYZ" TO REC
    MOVE CORRESPONDING OTHER-REC TO REC
    DISPLAY REC LIST.
SHOW-TOTAL.
    DISPLAY TOTAL
    MOVE "Z" TO REC-KEY IN REC
    STRING "Q" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO REC-KEY IN REC
    DISPLAY REC-KEY IN REC
    GOBACK.
